==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|secure|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/səˈkjʊɹli/|/səˈkjɝli/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/səˈkjʊəli/|/səˈkjɔːli/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-securely.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyph|en|se|cure|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{lb|en|manner}} In a [[secure]] manner; without fear or [[apprehension]]; without [[danger]].
#: {{syn|en|safely}}
#: {{ux|en|Check all personal items are '''securely''' stowed in the overhead lockers.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1919|author=Ellen N. La Motte|title=Peking Dust|chapter=|edition=|url=http://www.gutenberg.org/etext/26162
|passage=A square seat, about as wide and unyielding as a table-top, was strapped '''securely''' to each donkey, and to this seat we clung, with no secureness at all.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|author=Jacob L. Gewirtz; William M. Kurtines; Jacob L. Lamb|title=Intersections With Attachment|page=15
|passage=Only 5% of '''securely''' attached male subjects showed subsequent psychopathology compared to 40% of the insecurer attached males.}}

